{"canonical_record":{"canonical_payload_sha256":"a77355534ad57bf78b5e8e4d6e2b9a18dc92d52f531ccefa517b88a93eed48aa","full_review_record_id":"fullrev_eb8751d3514aa3bac5f2f5f2718d89ba0c1bd18a19d618a88fd8a823e243f1be","overall_assessment":"The paper presents a novel neural architecture (Relation Networks) for object-relation reasoning using synthetic data. The supplied evidence is insufficient to determine specific policy compliance regarding anonymity, plagiarism, or broader impact, as the paper lacks a dedicated policy section and the venue's specific 2017 policies are not provided. The data usage is compliant with privacy norms as it involves synthetic data, and the authors explicitly commit to making the datasets freely available.","paper_id":"Bk2TqVcxe","paper_identity_sha256":"22bec57e66dc4c72bb207aeed6142e5d72832a1f31e0fe462f5581bce78ba7f7","prompt_identity_sha256":"1cb318a3848106a240dade1d3c9447417cdf31200ac242d0c15ddf97f5371b69","raw_response_sha256":"c171d493b9e1cb02ce5683d1a8ee647cace7daaaa9f5df6508c0021b10f96484","request_identity_sha256":"bde64251b525944659ad3b29f868101052007e07e11d18565067eb8af4c0f2d9","reviewer_identity_sha256":"32b29c26fbf1508e066dfb25b1a9a3fe0654c5869a7da3020e1e8e61940befe3","role":"POL","schema_version":"agentreview-full-review-corpus-v4","structural_context_sha256":"ccc3402269162e33fac40eadd25cfb5ddca130127430d84df220ea28484452d5","subdimension_sections":[{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not contain a dedicated section discussing ethical risks, fairness, bias, or potential harms associated with the proposed Relation Networks architecture. The work focuses on synthetic scene classification and one-shot learning tasks, which do not present immediate, material ethical risks to marginalized populations or dual-use concerns visible in the text. However, the absence of any discussion on the broader ethical implications of the model's capabilities or limitations is noted.","subdimension_id":"POL-ETH"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-005","SRC-014"],"review_text":"The paper utilizes synthetic scene description data generated by hierarchical probabilistic generative models, as well as image depictions of these synthetic scenes. No human, personal, sensitive, or restricted data is used. The authors explicitly state that the datasets will be made freely available, which supports data transparency and reuse. There are no visible privacy violations or licensing conflicts regarding the synthetic data.","subdimension_id":"POL-DAT"},{"paper_anchor_ids":["SRC-001","SRC-035"],"review_text":"The paper lists author names, institutional affiliation (DeepMind, London, United Kingdom), and email addresses on the title page. The acknowledgments section thanks specific individuals and the DeepMind team. While these details identify the authors and their affiliation, the supplied evidence does not include the specific anonymity policy of the venue (ICLR 2017) to determine if this constitutes a violation of double-blind review rules. Therefore, a policy violation cannot be declared based solely on the paper text.","subdimension_id":"POL-ANO"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The supplied evidence does not contain information regarding plagiarism, self-plagiarism, or dual submission. The paper cites relevant prior work, such as Interaction Networks and Memory-Augmented Neural Networks, appropriately. Without access to external plagiarism databases or submission history, it is not possible to verify the originality of the content or the absence of duplicate submissions.","subdimension_id":"POL-PLG"},{"paper_anchor_ids":[],"review_text":"The paper does not include a broader impact statement, a responsible AI checklist, or explicit documentation of software/data licenses beyond the statement that datasets will be made freely available. There is no mention of IRB or ethics approval, which is consistent with the use of synthetic data. The absence of a dedicated broader impact section is noted, but without a frozen policy obligation from the venue, this cannot be declared a compliance failure.","subdimension_id":"POL-IMP"}]},"disposition":"CANONICAL_FULL_REVIEW_COMMITTED","item_commit_sha256":"9c80760e17847395a5986fd956500a4978d62dfb8b8fd3715f924412bea8039c","paper_id":"Bk2TqVcxe","paper_ordinal":43,"raw_attempts":[{"assistant_content_base64":"","assistant_content_sha256":"c171d493b9e1cb02ce5683d1a8ee647cace7daaaa9f5df6508c0021b10f96484","attempt_index":0,"error":"","finish_reason":"stop","paper_id":"Bk2TqVcxe","raw_provider_response_base64":"","raw_provider_response_sha256":"4a9c6850b7d4506990d8a8522c398d60a9bee2b4350e4ebefd4d87e7a6d1505b","request_identity_sha256":"bde64251b525944659ad3b29f868101052007e07e11d18565067eb8af4c0f2d9","role":"POL","schema_version":"no-memory-full-review-corpus-build-v6","usage":{"completion_tokens":750,"prompt_tokens":16099,"prompt_tokens_details":null,"total_tokens":16849},"valid":true}],"request_identity_sha256":"bde64251b525944659ad3b29f868101052007e07e11d18565067eb8af4c0f2d9","role":"POL","role_ordinal":4,"schema_version":"corpus-build-bootstrap-checkpoint-v4"}